s designated by surgeon as anterior  a long stitch is designated by surgeon as lateral  and a bowtie is designated by surgeon as cephalad  There is a needle localization wire in the anterior aspect of the specimen  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  lateral orange  medial yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an ill defined tan white firm rubbery area at the region of the localization wire that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm and focal areas of brown discoloration and hemorrhage  It appears to be grossly 0 2cm from the anterior  blue  margin at the medial aspect  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODES  A  Representative section of mass with closest margin  anterior and medial margins   B  Section immediately next to A  C F  Remainder of lesion  G H  Representative sections of fibrous areas away from mass  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast additional shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty breast tissue  There are stitches on one aspect designated by surgeon as the new margin  This new margin is inked black and the other opposite surface is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no gross lesions  The entire specimen is submitted sequentially in I CC  Resident  SARAH ROLLINS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   SHAVED MARGIN , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 55 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BBREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor grows as a dominant nodule spanning 0 6cm and several scattered small nests and cell clusters  Together they probably aggregate to 1 0cm or less  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 53                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of oriented breast  The superior resection margin is inked red  the inferior blue  the anterior green  the deep  posterior  inked yellow  and the medial and lateral are inked black  Sectioned to show white plugs extruding from ducts and a focally firm area  approximately 0 5cm in greatest dimension   Submitted entirely in A G  from medial to lateral  with the suspicious lesion in cassette D  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS EXAM  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Timothy Edward Guiney  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
