eled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan pink lymph node that is bivalved and entirely frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a long black stitch designating the 12 o clock aspect  On the anterior aspect of the specimen is a 9 5cm in length by 6 0cm in width skin ellipse with a 4 5cm eccentrically placed areola  that contains a 1 5cm diameter unremarkable appearing nipple  The specimen is inked anterior blue  posterior black and sectioned to reveal multiple cystic areas  with cysts measuring up to 3 0cm in diameter filled with dark green to pale yellow fluid  The remaining breast parenchyma is firm with scattered diffuse tan white fibrous tissue admixed with softer yellow adipose tissue  No axillary lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant with cyst wall and posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant with posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and cyst in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant with posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast stitch at 12 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the 12 o clock aspect  On the anterior surface there is an 8 0cm in length by 5 5cm in width skin ellipse that contains a 5 0cm in diameter areola with a central unremarkable 1 5cm nipple  The specimen is inked anterior blue  posterior black and serially sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm firm area in the deep upper inner quadrant of the right breast  The firm area has a multilobular architecture with firm  red areas containing punctate firm  white papules scattered amongst more pale yellow with wispy white fibroadipose tissue  The firm area approaches to within 0 5cm from the posterior margin located in the upper inner quadrant  The mass comes to within 5 0cm of the superior aspect of the margin  6 0cm from the lateral aspect to the margin  15 0cm from the inferior aspect of the specimen  15 0cm from the lateral aspect of the specimen  and approaches to within 0 8cm of the anterior margin which consists of the nipple  Ten representative sections of the firm area are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The posterior margin is included in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and suspected biopsy site in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two representative sections of the lower inner quadrant are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   two representative sections of the lower outer quadrant are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   two representative sections of the upper outer quadrant are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and representative sections of areola to underlying breast tissue are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross Dictation by Stewart M Knoepp M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Stewart M Knoepp M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Christine Garcia M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor 