Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 58 CLINICAL DATA  44 year old female  excision of right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2 5CM  GRADE 3 OF 3  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED RESECTION MARGINS  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The larger piece is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  firm  gritty  tan white mass with central foci of yellow discoloration  several  each 0 1cm in greatest dimension   present at multiple inked margins  Representative section frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassettes B F  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST MASS   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
