Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  02 MAY 96 at 13 16 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE I  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  EXTENDING AWAY FROM MASS AND TO THE MARGIN OF SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 MAY 96 at 13 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 MAY 96 at 16 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy specimen and localizing wire  The specimen has been inked and sectioned to reveal a firm grey white 0 9cm area  Frozen section is done  The specimen is submitted in total in cassette A through G with suspicious area in cassettes A through C  Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  FIRM AREA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Masha Jannine Etkin  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 23 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  CARCINOSARCOMA WITH FOCAL CARTILAGINOUS AND OSSEOUS DIFFERENTIATION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is composed of both malignant epithelial and mesenchymal  sarcomatous  areas  These two components are distinct and do not show any merging from the carcinoma into the sarcoma  Immunoperoxidase stains confirm divergent differentiation  with cytokeratins being positive only in the epithelial areas and vimentin and desmin only in the sarcomatous regions  S 100 only stains the carcinoma  Although the differential diagnosis includes a metaplastic carcinoma with extensive sarcomatous areas  there is usually more blending of the epithelial and mesenchymal areas in metaplastic carcinoma  Also  immunoperoxidase usually shows some keratin positivity in the sarcomatous areas in a metaplastic carcinoma  Another interesting feature in this case is that the background of this tumor is reminiscent of a phylloides tumor  with broad stromal fronds focally covered by malignant epithelium  This feature raises the possibility that this tumor is arising in a high grade phylloides  All margins are greater than 0 2cm  No angiolymphatic invasion is seen  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the case and agrees with this interpretation  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 13 15                                                                                     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     ADDENDUM  ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION   The tumor size is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm  see gross description   No lymph nodes were identified in the axillary tail  Sections taken from this region also do not reveal lymph nodes  Added by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  18 MAY 00 at 16 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm right modified radical mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm tan wrinkled skin ellipse and a 2 9cm symmetrical nipple areolar complex  A short suture designates superior and long suture designates the axillary tail per the surgeon  There is a 5 5cm well healed curvilinear scar approximately 5 0cm lateral to the areola  The specimen is inked black and serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm well demarcated tan red  focally necrotic mass which comes within 2 7cm of the posterior margin of resection  closest margin  and approximately 0 5cm from the skin  Approximately 1 5cm superior posterior to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm area of skin wedge  The posterior margin is retracted  Sectioning of this area reveals tan white fibrous tissue  A mass cannot grossly be identified in this area  The remaining breast tissue reveals approximately 65  yellow adipose tissue and 35  tan white unremarkable fibrous stroma  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail is present containing no definite lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A D  Tumor  E  Posterior resection margin adjacent to tumor  F  Posterior margin  area of retraction  G  Random breast tissue  H J  Possible lymph nodes from axillary tail  Gross Description by  DELIA FINNIE Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Danielle D Elliott  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Pathologic_size.
