Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  29 AUG 95 at 11 46 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOLID TYPE WITH HIGH GRADE CYTOLOGIC FEATURES  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  NOTE  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The infiltrating carcinoma is composed of predominantly single cells in an  indian file pattern  and with rare invasive glands  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of unremarkable breast tissue  A radiogram is also included  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through J  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  NO FROZEN DONE  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
