F MALIGNANCY   SEE NOTE     NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically  evaluated       LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE   SEE NOTE     NOTE  To evaluate for metastatic carcinoma  immunohistochemical stains for  cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin were examined on levels  from each of three blocks  The findings support the above diagnosis       GROSS DESCRIPTION   Unfixed  labeled  Rosalyn Tabasky  REMOVED_DATE  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  3 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with two localization wires  a short suture  designating the superior margin  and a long suture designating the lateral  margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the medial  green  and the lateral yellow  There is a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm elongated  region of hemorrhage surrounded by chalky yellow tissue  The hemorrhagic area  is firm and extends to 0 7cm from the medial margin  1 3cm from the anterior  margin  1 1cm from the posterior margin  0 4cm from the lateral margin  and  more than 2 0cm from the superior and inferior margins  Representative  sections are submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the  entire hemorrhagic area in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      In fixative  labeled  Rosalyn Tabasky  REMOVED_DATE  medial margin  left breast    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm piece of focally hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue with a  suture designating the new margin  which is inked  The specimen is entirely  submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      In fixative  labeled  Rosalyn Tabasky  REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin  left breast    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with a suture  designating the new margin  which is inked  The specimen is entirely submitted  in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      In fixative  labeled  Rosalyn Tabasky  REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin  left  breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm piece of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with  a suture designating the new margin  which is inked  The specimen is entirely  submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Unfixed  in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Rosalyn Tabasky  REMOVED_DATE   195 53 47 and  left sentinel lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink  lymph node  which is bisected  entirely frozen as FX 1  and submitted in  cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining tissue is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS   FROZEN SECTION  1   LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA     Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on  Wednesday May 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 28 44AM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     PART A  Breast  Left   Excision  PART B  Breast  Left   Medial Margin    Excision  PART C  Breast  Left   Lateral Margin    Excision  PART D  Breast  Left   Posterior Margin    Excision  PART E  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel    Excision  PART F  Cryostat Frozen Section  slide only        report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  FIBROADENOMA  INVOLUTED  WITH EXTENSIVE MICROCALCIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  A   RIGHT   BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FIBROSIS  CYSTS  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  AND EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  B   RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60    WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE MM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  40    SEE NOTE  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma extends to an inked margin  Definite lymphatic invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  David Weissmann  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 21 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  B    THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  with a localizing wire and x ray showing clusters of coarse calcifications at one margin  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an area of white gray  gritty tissue  abutting an inked margin  0 4 x 0 2cm    No frozen section done  Suspicious areas in cassettes A through C  rest in D through I  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Labeled   1  right breast specimen A  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place and x ray demonstrating clusters of large coarse calcifications  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm cluster of white gray gritty material abutting an inked margin  No frozen section done  The specimen is too small to freeze  Lesion submitted in cassettes J  K and the remainder submitted entirely in cassettes L through Q  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast  B  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place  an x ray demonstrating vague radio density at one end of the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a gray pink gritty fairly well circumscribed nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm extending to within 0 2cm of the inked margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  The lesion is submitted in cassettes R through V  the remainder is submitted entirey in cassettes W through GG  No frozen done  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT   NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST A  BIOPSY  NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST B  BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  NO FROZEN SECTION DONE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Simon Bergman  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST PART B  RIGHT BREAST A PART C  RIGHT BREAST B   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
