Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  1 3CM  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  1   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR AND INFERIOR RESECTION MARGINS   SEE NOTE  2   INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  NOTE  1  No blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  NOTE  2  No stromal  blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  MICROCALCIFICATIONS ASSOCIATED WITH BENIGN DUCTS  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 45                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     ADDENDUM  Immunohistochemical stains on formalin fixed paraffin embedded tissue shows the tumor cells are strongly positive for neuron specific enolase  faintly positive for synoptophysin  and negative for chromogranin  These findings are suggestive of carcinoma with neuroendocrine features  Added by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 30     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast  is an unoriented breast biopsy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The superior margin is inked black  the inferior is inked blue  and the anterior surface is overinked green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm white firm  stellate area in the lateral half of the specimen  coming within 0 4cm from the closest resection margin  superior   Representative section of the stellate area is frozen as FX 1 and is resubmitted in cassette A  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes B J  Tumor is in B F  Lateral half in G and H  and medial half in I and J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregular portion of breast tissue with a suture on one aspect marking the edge farthest from the tumor  The sutured half is black  the opposite blue  Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no discrete lesions  Specimen is entirely submitted in K S  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  DR  GADD SAW THE SPECIMEN IN THE FROZEN SECTION LAB  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPS   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 12 CLINICAL DATA  Excision breast lesion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  98   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  2   CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The focus of infiltrating carcinoma measures 0 7cm on the slide  The surgical resection margins are free of tumor  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying x ray of the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 8cm ill defined  soft  red tan area extending to within 0 2cm of the inked margin  adjacent to the thick end of wire  The remaining parenchyma is composed of soft  lobulated  unremarkable adipose tissue  The nodule is submitted in A F  The adjacent parenchyma and firmer areas from the remaining parenchyma are submitted in G O  Resident  Asif Rashid  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT EXCISION  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESION THAT IS LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  George S Richardson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST LESION   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
