Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 55 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   90    WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    CRIBRIFORM TYPE MULTIFOCAL  BOTH WITHIN AND OUTSIDE OF THE INVASIVE COMPONENT SEE NOTE  NOTE  The invasive tumor measures 1 1cm in greatest diameter on histologic section  slide A  and approaches to within 0 4cm of the inked resection margin  A separate focus of invasive carcinoma is present 0 1cm from a resection margin  slide F   Carcinoma in situ is present less than 0 1cm from the closest inked margin  slides B  C  E   There is no definite vascular or lymphatic invasion identified  Multiple levels examined  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 4 x 4 x 2 5cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue with a palpable firm nodule  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 x 0 6cm white  gritty  stellate area that approaches the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remaining specimen is submitted entirely in A through K  with the nodule in A C  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT BIOPSY  INFILTRATING and INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
