Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  John Dekker  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Revised Report            Reason for Amendment  1  Corrected Transcription Error not in Final Diagnosis CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 52 year old woman with a recent diagnosis of invasive breast cancer who has undergone neoadjuvant chemotherapy  She now presents for a right breast lumpectomy  short superior  long lateral  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  See table 1 and note  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  Microscopic foci  See note  GRADE  3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to   0 1cm from the anterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within  and beyond  the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ is positive at the superior  anterior and lateral margins of the specimen along broad fronts  NOTE  The tumor is present as multiple small microscopic nests and trabeculae as well as single tumor cells in a background of dense sclerosis  This finding likely reflects prior chemotherapy with near complete resolution of the tumor mass  Immunohistochemical stains for p63  myosin  calponin and cytokeratin were performed on sections  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Although limited by sectioning artifact  the immunohistochemical stains support the diagnosis of residual invasive ductal carcinoma  The DCIS is present on at least 8 of 10 sections of the breast  The diagnosis of DCIS is complicated by the affect of prior neoadjuvant chemotherapy which accentuates the cytologic atypia in the areas of DCIS  Notably a field defect with changes in benign ductal cells is not observed  We considered the possibility that the cytologic changes are purely artifactual and secondary to the chemotherapy  rather than representing residual DCIS  However  the degree of cytological atypia in the involved ducts as well as the extent of the changes and the presence of architectural abnormalities strongly favors a diagnosis of DCIS  An immunohistochemical stain for keratin REMOVED_DATE performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  shows focal staining in luminal ductal cells  however  we interpret this finding as nonspecific in the setting of neoadjuvant chemotherapy  Overall  the findings are interpreted as residual invasive and in situ ductal carcinoma in the setting of prior neoadjuvant chemotherapy  Dr  Melinda Lerwill has reviewed this case and concurs with the diagnosis  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   is a lumpectomy specimen oriented by 2 sutures measuring 4 8cm x 3 6cm x 1 1cm  The specimen is inked anterior black  posterior   blue  medial  green  lateral   yellow  A needle localization wire is present and an x ray is provided demonstrating the positions of 2 metal clips relative to the wire  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal tan white nodular breast tissue with areas of hemorrhage  The helical clip is identified in one section and adjacent to this clip is a tan firm mass embedded in white fibrous tissue  The mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and is located 0 5cm from the closest anterior margin  0 5cm from the closest medial margin  1 4cm from the closest posterior margin  1 6cm from the closest lateral margin  1 6cm from the closest superior margin  2 0cm from the closest inferior margin  The second S shaped clip is not identified  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First superior section taken after en face margin  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Next section  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Next section containing white fibrous areas divided into 3 pieces   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor with closest black inked anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor with closest green medial margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of uninvolved breast  Amended report  1  Corrected transcription error not in final diagnosis  This report has been revised to correct a transcription error in Table  1  The prior report had the statement  cannot evaluate  under the headings of invasive and in situ carcinoma  We have deleted these statements and specified the margins for DCIS  The prior report should be disregarded  Dr  Michele Specht was notified of the changes on REMOVED_DATE at 9 30 am  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment  1 by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   Breast  Right   Excision  report_end  , Pathologic_size.
