ls stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain faintly for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  92  to chromosome 17 signals  87  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  RIGHT POSTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART F  BREAST  RIGHT MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART G  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SE  report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Resident  Anna McDonald  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Revised Report            Reason for Amendment  1  Corrected Final Diagnosis Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Amendment  2  Corrected Transcription Error not in Final Diagnosis CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 60 year old woman with left breast enhancement seen on MRI  A prior core biopsy demonstrated probable lobular neoplasia  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  EXTENSIVE LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  WITH CALCIFICATIONS   SEE TABLE 1 AND NOTE   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  DCIS  TUMOR SIZE  Involving 4 of 6 blocks  GRADE  3  CALCIFICATIONS  Limited to the carcinoma in situ  Both LCIS and DCIS   MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive along the inked margin of the specimen along a broad front  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Sections of the excision sample reveal large ducts distended by tumor cells  In many areas the tumor cells are large and pleomorphic with abundant cytoplasm and occasional single mucin vacuoles  A few cells have a signet ring appearance  The nuclei are mildly enlarged with mildly irregular contours and granular chromatin  The morphologic findings in these areas are compatible with pleomorphic variant of lobular carcinoma in situ  Intermixed with these areas are other ducts with cells that have a similar appearance but with a distinctly cribriform pattern compatible with a component of DCIS  An immunohistochemical stain for E cadherin on Slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is largely negative and supports the diagnosis of LCIS  however  there is weak membrane staining in the ductal cells in the areas of cribriform architecture supporting a diagnosis DCIS  Stains for p63  myosin  calponin and keratin performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  do not show evidence of an invasive carcinoma  Overall  the morphologic findings are compatible with carcinoma in situ with both ductal and lobular features  Immunostains for estrogen receptor and progesterone receptor will be reported in an addendum  This case was amended to correct the final diagnosis  On initial review  the findings were interpreted as extensive LCIS  However  upon review of the e cadherin as well as the ER  PR and Her 2neu stain the findings were interpreted as both ductal and lobular carcinoma in situ  The final diagnosis and note in the report has been revised to reflect these changes  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Donovan  REMOVE_MRN and  left breast needle loc   is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue  5 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6   with two needle localization wires in place  The specimen is entirely inked black and serially sectioned to reveal no mass lesions  The specimen is entirely included in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with   prior biopsy site in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Amended report This report was amended to correct the acronym in the title of the table of pathologic findings  The acronym previously listed as  LCIS  has been changed to  DCIS   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment  1 by Ronald Balassanian M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment  2 by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  report_end  , Pathologic_size.
