Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 11 CLINICAL DATA  History of radiation for Hodgkin s age 18 now with left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  FORMING MULTIPLE NODULES THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE NUCLEAR GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  No blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  In areas  the invasive component has features of invasive lobular carcinoma  SKIN  RIGHT NIPPLE   BIOPSY  ACROCHORDON  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 19 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   A few tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm breast biopsy that is inked and sectioned to reveal a slightly nodular and cystic breast parenchyma  submitted entirely in A H  Labeled with the patients name  unit number and  right nipple skin tag   is an unoriented fragment of soft tissue measuring 0 5cm in greatest diameter that is inked  bisected and submitted entirely in I  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST   NO LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY PART B  SKIN  RIGHT NIPPLE    BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
