Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  10 MAY 95 at 13 24 CLINICAL DATA  Breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   2  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 11 OF 11 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  3  SKIN SCAR WITH FAT NECROSIS CONSISTENT WITH PREVIOUS BIOPSY  4  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  5  DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  6  RADIAL SCAR  7  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  AND APROCRINE METAPLASIA  NOTE  The tumor measures grossly 2 5cm in greatest dimension  The resection margins are free of tumor  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 95 at 15 21                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with axillary tail  An overlying skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm  and contains a 2 0cm nipple 8 0cm from the medial ellipse margin  A 3 5cm long well healed linear scar is present in the upper outer quadrant  1 0cm from the superior lateral ellipse margin  Multiple hard axillary lymph nodes are palpable immediately deep to this scar  This specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm pink tan  firm  well demarcated nodule with infiltrative borders  This nodule is 1 0cm from the medial inked margin  1 0cm deep to the skin  and 5 0cm from the nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm ill defined  fibrous region with focal nodularity is continuous with this nodule  and focally abuts the superior posterior inked margin  Multiple  smooth  pink tan  hard nodules measuring up to 1 0cm in greatest dimension are identified in this fibrous region  which are suggestive of intraparenchymal lymph nodes  The region immediately deep to the skin scar contains focal fat necrosis and fibrosis  but no biopsy cavity is identified  Eleven hard axillary lymph nodes measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm in greatest dimension are identified  Section code  A B  Nodule near medial resection margin C E  Nodule  additional sections F  Skin scar and deep fat necrosis G L  Ill defined fibrous region with nodules  H I abutting inked posterior superior margin  M  Lymph nodes  5  N  Lymph nodes  6  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  ELLISON 07 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , Pathologic.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  75   MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  25   BOTH COMPONENTS FOCALLY EXTENDING TO INKED MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Both invasive and in situ components of the tumor approach to within less than 0 1cm of several inked margins  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The main tumor mass grossly measures 1 0cm in greatest dimension  and includes both in situ and invasive tumor  Foci of in situ carcinoma are also present well apart from the main tumor mass  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  more invasive areas were present on additional sections than on the section frozen for intraoperative evaluation  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty breast tissue fragment with localizing wire and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a fairly well circumscribed 1 0cm rubbery  pink tan to white focus abutting several inked margins  representative section of lesion is frozen as frozen section  1  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A E  The frozen is submitted in cassette F  No BRDU or estrogen and progesterone receptors are sent  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  RULE OUT INVASION  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
