Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 AUG 96 ACCESSIONED ON  14 AUG 96 at 11 49 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT BREAST MASS    BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE III III   PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES AND WITH MULTIFOCAL LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma is present extensively throughout the entire specimen  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The intraoperative gross diagnosis is confirmed  SKIN  BREAST  LEFT   SPECIMEN LOST IN PATHOLOGY DEPARTMENT  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  20 AUG 96 at 10 22 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 96 at 09 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm portion of fibrofatty tissue and an accompanying radiograph  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  stellate  ill defined  firm  white area which is at the margin  No frozen is performed  The specimen is submitted entirely with the stellate region in cassettes A through E  remaining tissue is submitted entirely in cassette F  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST MASS   FIRM TISSUE SUSPICIOUS FOR MALIGNANCY  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST SKIN  LEFT  PART B  BREAST AND CALCIFICATION  LEFT    report_end  , Pathologic_size.
