Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 37 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma of the right breast and ductal carcinoma in situ in the left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MODERATE GRADE  PRESENT IN 1 OF 7 REPRESENTATIVE TISSUE BLOCKS  DISTANT FROM THE RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MULTIFOCAL  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION TO SUTURE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  NOTE  No stromal  blood vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  ASSOCIATED WITH AND AWAY FROM THE BIOPSY CAVITY   SEE NOTE  NOTE  All resection margins are free of invasive and in situ carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma forms 3 major masses  2 2cm  1 4cm and 1 0cm  Multiple smaller foci of invasive tumor associated with in situ carcinoma are also present  Invasive carcinoma is focally present 0 1cm from a deep resection margin  The invasive and in situ carcinomas display ductal and lobular features  The invasive ductal component is low grade  grade REMOVED_DATE No blood vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  IN SITU CARCINOMA  WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  EXTENSIVE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA PRESENT IN 2 OF 17 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  One of the lymph nodes contains more than 0 2cm of metastatic carcinoma distributed in the subcapsular sinus  Another lymph node contains scattered nests of tumor cells which are less than 0 2cm in agggregate  Positive keratin stains confirm these findings  SOFT TISSUE  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are three specimens  Labelled  left modified radical mastectomy   is a mastectomy specimen with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  On the skin ellipse there is also a 2 9cm long vertical well healed scar  The areola on the skin ellipse measures 2 9cm in diameter and has a nipple in the center with 1 2cm diameter  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating the superior margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm biopsy cavity located below the well healed scar  The cavity is 0 5cm from the closest posterior resection margin  Around the biopsy cavity is relatively firm white yellow fibrous tissue  The inferior to the cavity there is a well circumscribed white 3 5cm in greatest diameter firm nodule  which is 0 2cm from the posterior  deep  margin  The remaining breast parenchyma appears grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are taken  Submitted in cassette A G  Section code  A  Biopsy cavity and nodule in relation to closest  deep  resection margin  B  Nodule C E  Biopsy cavity with adjacent nodule in relation to resection margin  F  Nodule G  Unremarkable breast parenchyma  representative section  In the axillary tail a suture designates the axillary nodes and in this area two lymph nodes are found  One lymph node measure 1 3cm in greatest diameter  the other 1 6cm in greatest diameter  The lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes H I  Additionally  two lymph nodes were also found in the axillary tail and are submitted in cassette J  Labelled  right modified radical mastectomy   is a mastectomy specimen with a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the superior margin  On the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse which has a 2 5cm in diameter areola centered by a 1 3cm nipple  A vertical scar measuring 2 3cm in length  well healed  is located at the supra lateral portion of the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity with an adjacent REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm gritty nodule is superior to the biopsy cavity  The biopsy cavity is 0 4cm from the anterior superior inked margin  The biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm and is 0 3cm from the deep margin  about 3cm inferior to the biopsy cavity there is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm white firm ill defined mass which is present 0 1cm from the deep margin  In addition  there is a firm 1 2cm nodule at the lateral end of the biopsy cavity  Section code  K  First nodule in relation to closest margin  L P  Biopsy cavity with adjacent second nodule  inferior nodule  in relation to deep margin  Second nodule and deep margin  Q  Third nodule  lateral  R Z  Lymph nodes Labelled  additional right axillary tissue   consists of three fragments of yellow adipose tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and is submitted entirely in cassette W  Resident  RICHARD AMMER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W P Andrew Lee  M D  Bruce Allan Chabner  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART C  SOFT TISSUE  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION , Pathologic.
