Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 40 CLINICAL DATA  Known  presumed  metastatic gastric carcinoma  treated with chemotherapy  Known left breast cancer  Now with right breast mass and   left supraclavicular lymph node                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  RIGHT LATERAL  1   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH LOBULAR CARCINOMA PRESENT IN 7 OF 8 TISSUE SECTIONS  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The largest single tumor dimension on one slide is 1 4cm  However  the tumor is probably much larger since it is present in 7 of 8 tissue sections  The tumor cells are positive for ER  negative for PR and focally positive for GCDFP  Definite in situ carcinoma is not seen  The overall cytology  morphology and immunoperoxidase reactivity are consistent with invasive lobular carcinoma  However  in the absence of an in situ component  one can not completely rule out a gastric metastasis  The slides of the previous gastric carcinoma were not available for review  B  BREAST  RIGHT BREAST  2  CENTRAL   EXCISION  INVASIVE CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH LOBULAR CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite in situ component is not seen Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  C  BREAST  RIGHT ADDITIONAL MARGIN  2   EXCISION  INVASIVE CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH LOBULAR CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  PRESENT AT THE MARGIN DESIGNATED BY THE BLACK STITCH AND THE OPPOSITE MARGIN   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The foci of carcinoma each average 0 2cm in overall dimension  Definite in situ carcinoma is not seen  D  LYMPH NODE  LEFT SUPRACLAVICULAR   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH BREAST