Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 12 13 CLINICAL DATA  70 y o  female with right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  CONSISTENT WITH EXTRANODAL MARGINAL ZONE B CELL LYMPHOMA  NOTE  Sections show a large mass lesion composed of a dense  diffuse to vaguely nodular  rather monotonous infiltrate of small lymphoid cells with slightly irregular nuclei with a small amount of clear cytoplasm  with scattered plasma cells and rare small aggregates of follicle center cells  The infiltrate abuts on the margin  The histologic features are consistent with marginal zone B cell lymphoma  and immunohistochemical studies support this interpretation  see addendum   Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 08                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibodies to immunoglobulin light chains there is polytypic staining of many plasma cells  With antibodies to B lineage antigen s    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  staining reveals extensive networks of dendritic cells  With antibodies to T lineage associated antigen s    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of small cells scattered within the tissue  Lymphocytes in rare aggregates are also positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   consistent with residual follicle centers  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results support the diagnosis of extranodal marginal zone B cell lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm predominantly yellow lobulated fibrofatty portion of unoriented breast notable for 2 wires flanking a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm slightly firm area  The specimen is black inked bivalved to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm pink gray firm ill defined area and the remainder predominantly yellow lobulated fatty parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted  SECTION CODES  A C  The entire ill defined pink area  D   Unremarkable parenchyma  Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Pathologic_size.
