Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 14 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  4 CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 3 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor cells transgresses the capsule of one lymph node to slightly invade the axillary fat  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   ADDITIONAL    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast tissue  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm with a grossly unremarkable nipple  An attached axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Sectioning reveals a white  hard lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm which grossly approaches the deep margin which is the closest margin to 0 2cm  Section code  AandB  lesion and deep margin C G  representative sections of lesion H L  lymph nodes from axillary tail Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  additional axillary tissue  is a single piece of fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Submitted in toto in cassette M  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
