Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  20 AUG 97 at 14 52 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  TWO SEPARATE TUMORS  2 5 AND REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIAMETER   BOTH GRADE 3  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  COMEDO TYPE  EXTENSIVELY INVOLVING BROAD AREAS AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE TUMOR NODULES  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Lymphatic invasion is identified  The larger nodule is 0 2cm from the deep margin  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  REGIONAL DISSECTION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITHIN 12 OF 15 LYMPH NODES  WITH EARLY EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION FROM ONE NODE  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  22 AUG 97 at 18 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   Both Masses  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labelled with the patient name  unit number and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple  Suture marking indicates superior  The specimen is inked black anteriorly and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm firm  yellow white mass with irregular borders that is located 0 2cm from the nearest deep margin  The mass is eccentrically located in the inferior external quadrant  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm soft  white yellow multilobulated lesion with bluish cystic spaces and solid areas are identified eccentrically in the lateral superior quadrant of the breast several centimeters from the main tumor  Representative tissue section through the tumor are included in cassette A G  Section C includes the nearest margin  Representative section through the second lesion are included through cassette H L  Section away from the tumor are included in M   N  The specimen also includes an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibroadipose tissue containing lymph nodes  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted through cassettes 0 R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY , Pathologic_size.
