ist s   MELINDA J  FAN  MD     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block W   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  02 AUG 01 at 06 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a 24 x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm simple mastectomy with attached axillary tissue  with an overlying ellipse of skin measuring 18 x 7 0cm  There is a well healed scar measuring 3 0cm curving around the medial edge of the unremarkable nipple  areolar complex  The surgeon has oriented the specimen with a stitch on the axillary tail  The entire specimen is inked in black  Serial sectioning reveals a 3 x 2 x 1cm biopsy cavity 0 2cm from the deep margin  with surrounding firm  tan white fibrous parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A E  Biopsy cavity F G  Parenchyma deep to nipple H L  Away from biopsy cavity P Y  Biopsy cavity and adjacent parenchyma  with ink representing deep margin Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE to 1 1cm in greatest dimension  They are submitted as follows  M  Two lymph nodes  each bisected N  Two lymph nodes  each bisected O  Three whole lymph nodes  Resident  ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DA