ive percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of breast tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ellipse of unremarkable overlying skin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 9cm in greatest diameter white tan  hard scirrhous nodule grossly involving the resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and kept frozen for Cox 5  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassettes A through D  with cassette A having the majority of the nodule  The skin is submitted in D  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  Carlos Fernandez del castillo  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
