Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 14 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   1   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  98   TWO NODULES  THE LARGER REMOVED_DATE CM IN MAXIMUM DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION   EXTENDING TO A RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  2   HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  INVOLVING ONE DUCT SITUATED ONE HIGH POWER FIELD FROM THE LARGER TUMOR MASS  NOTE  Neither lymphatic nor blood vessel invasion is present  The intra operative gross impression is confirmed  BREAST  LEFT   2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  FOCAL MILD DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  2  LUMENAL MICROCALCIFICATIONS  3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE INTRA OPERATIVE GROSS IMPRESSION IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  with needle localizing wire in place  and accompanying specimen x ray which shows calcifications  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal two white  firm  well demarcated nodules  that measure REMOVED_DATE and 0 3cm in greatest diameter  respectively  and are adjacent to the an inked resection margin  These lesions are two small to freeze and no frozen section is done  The specimen is submitted entirely in A through K  with the lesions in A through C  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 0cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue with needle localizing wire in place and accompanying specimen x ray which shows calcifications  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal fleshy yellow and white streaked soft breast tissue with no lesions suspicious for invasive carcinoma  No frozen section is done  The specimen is submitted entirely in L through R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY  TWO SUSPICIOUS FIRM AREAS  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENT SECTIONS  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BIOPSY WITH NEEDLE LOCALIZATION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY PART B  BIOPSY WITH NEEDLE LOCALIZATION   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
