terminations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of breast tissue with needle  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm white tan mass with a 1 0cm central cystic area  A representative section of tumor is frozen as fx 1 and saved frozen  The remaining tumor is submitted in cassettes A D with additional representative sections of normal breast in cassette E F  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  WITH APOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION , Pathologic_size.
