Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  05 AUG 98 at 13 04 CLINICAL DATA  Density on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  AT OR ABUTTING THE INKED MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  CONFINED TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  No angiolymphatic invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  07 AUG 98 at 19 43 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 AUG 98 at 14 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing guide wire  It is inked and sectioned to reveal a 2 0cm in diameter firm white nodule with irregular borders abutting the inked margins  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as FX 1  now in cassette A  The rest of the specimen entirely submitted in cassettes B through D  Gross Description by  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
