Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 05 CLINICAL DATA  69 year old female with invasive ductal carcinoma on a core biopsy  undergoing excision with axillary dissection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY SITE AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  Note  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  Lymphatic vessel and blood vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL TISSUE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 23 OF 23 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm breast excision specimen  The entire surface is inked black with the deep  posterior  margin overinked blue  and the superior margin overinked red  Serially sectioning the tissue reveals a hemorrhagic area  surrounded by an ill defined stellate  white  firm mass  with maximum diameter of 1 0cm  located in the center of the specimen  with fibrous extensions approaching the margins  The tissue away from this mass is almost entirely yellow fatty tissue with minimal fibrous strands  SECTION CODE A  FX  1  mass with superior margin  B  FX  2  mass with superficial margin  C  FX  3  mass with inferior margin  D  FX  4  mass with deep margin  E H  Remainder of the mass  I  Representative section of remainder of tissue  Designated  left breast  additional breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 1 5cm breast tissue  oriented by a short and long stitch designating the deep margin  two short stitches designating the medial margin  and two long stitches designating the superior margin  The entire excised surface is inked black with the superficial half overinked blue  Cross sectioning reveals an ill defined firm  white  fibrous areas abutting the superficial margin along a broad front  in the medial portion of the specimen  and focally abutting the new deep margin  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral in J through P  Designated  axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fatty tissue  from which multiple lymph nodes are extracted and submitted in Q through V  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SUPERIOR MARGIN   DIFFICULT TO INTERPRET DUE TO FREEZING ARTIFACT  NO OBVIOUS TUMOR SEEN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  SUPERFICIAL MARGIN   DIFFICULT TO INTERPRET DUE TO FREEZING ARTIFACT  NO OBVIOUS TUMOR SEEN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  3  INFERIOR MARGIN   DIFFICULT TO INTERPRET DUE TO FREEZING ARTIFACT  NO OBVIOUS TUMOR SEEN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  4  DEEP MARGIN   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  CANNOT EVALUATE MARGIN DUE TO FREEZING ARTIFACT  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL TISSUE   EXCISIONAL BIOPS PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  , Pathologic_size.
