Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 05 CLINICAL DATA  Fifty eight year old undergoing excision of left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    MUCINOUS  COLLOID  TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM MARGIN  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  PRESENT ADJACENT TO INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  un it number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast biopsy specimen with localizing wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm tan firm well circumscribed nodule adherent to grossly unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  A representative section is frozen as FX  1  resubmitted as cassette J  The rest of the specimen entirely submitted in cassettes A through I with nodule in cassettes A through C  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   COLLOID CARCINOMA  O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Pathologic_size.
