Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 52 CLINICAL DATA  83 year old female with a left breast lump                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 5cm    95  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION PRESENT  2 INTRA DUCTAL CARCINOMA AT INKED MARGINS  SOLID TYPE  5   3 FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST AND AXILLA  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 6   90   MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definite vascular invasion is identified  Inked resection margins are negative  There is no evidence of malignancy in REMOVED_DATE lymph nodes  2 INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  10   3 ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE FOCUS  Diagnosis by  Robert B  Colvin  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive 