Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 09 39 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma involving the dermis                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MICROFOCUS OF SINGLE TUMOR CELLS   0 1 CM   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  CALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  10 TOTAL  WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  NOTE  The entire biopsy site was microscopically examined as well as extensive sampling of skin and adjacent parenchyma  One slide containing invasive tumor cells was identified  The prior specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   was reviewed for comparison  Dr F  Koerner reviewed the residual invasive tumor slide and concurs  Diagnosis by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 12 03                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left MRM   is a 27 x 20 x 5cm modified radical mastectomy  There is a 19 x 6 5cm skin ellipse with a centrally located 4cm nipple areolar complex  No scars nor skin alterations are identified grossly   A 5 x 5 x 4cm axillary pad is attached to the specimen  The specimen is inked blue anteriorly and black posteriorly anteriorly sectioned to reveal a 5 x 5 x 4 5cm poorly defined fibrosed area with focal firmness below the nipple  The mass is 0 9cm from the anterior resection margin at the superior edge of the skin ellipse  The fibrous area extends laterally where it abuts the black inked resection margin  The remaining parenchyma shows a sclerosed firm area  1cm in diameter   1cm from the anterior and posterior margins and 3cm from the inferior margin of the level of the nipple  A 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fibrosed nodule is present 5cm from the lateral margin of the specimen where it abuts the posterior margin  The remaining parenchyma is constituted by lobulated adipose tissue with scattered non suspicious area of fibrous bands  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Mass  1 5cm away from the non represented black inked margin  C D  Superior aspect of the nipple and mass  1cm from the non represented black inked margin  E  Mass abutting the black inked margin  F G  Inferior portion of the mass  1 8cm from the black inked margin  H  Most lateral area of the mass abutting the black ink margin  I  Sclerosed firm area   1cm in diameter  J  2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fibrosed nodule  K  Four intact lymph nodes  L  Two bivalved lymph nodes  one inked black  M O  One bivalved lymph node per cassette  P  Bivalved matted area in the axillary sample  Q R  Bivalved matted area in the axillary sample  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Pathologic_size.
