Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 MAY 91 ACCESSIONED ON  10 MAY 91 at 17 10 CLINICAL DATA  81 year old female with right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   95    MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA   5    2  FIBROCYSTIC DISEASE  NOTE  Residual tumor within the biopsy cavity measures 2 0cm in greatest dimension  No vascular invasion is identified  The surgical resection margins are free of tumor  A single focus of intraductal carcinoma is present in breast tissue distal from the main tumor mass   slide I   LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 9 OUT OF 9 LYMPH NODES  SKIN  CHEST  EXCISION  DERMAL NEVUS WITH NEURATIZATION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Carolyn K  Pettit  M D  Signed On  16 MAY 91 at 18 26 Staff Pathologist  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  13 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Negative Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 17 09     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and site  Labeled  Right breast and axillary contents  is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gram  17 x 12 x 2cm breast and axillary tail  The overlying ellipse of skin measures 17 x 12cm with an eccentric unremarkable nipple  Serial sections of the breast parenchyma reveal a firm  gray white well defined mass measuring 2 x 1 x 1 9cm  which approaches to witin 0 9cm from the deep resection margin  Remaining breast parenchyma is soft and unremarkable  The axillary tail measures 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm and has multiple pink white soft lymph nodes 1 4cm in greatest dimension with homogeneous cut surfaces  A representative sample of the breast mass is taken in the frozen section lab and sent for biochemical estrogen receptor study  a portion is saved frozen for immunohistologic studies  Section Code  A  nipple  B C  tumor and deep margin  D G  tumor  H  adjacent breast  I  random breast  J L N  lymph nodes  In a second container labeled  Right chest skin lesion is a 0 5cm in diameter polypoid white soft skin mass  Bisected entirely in M  Resident  John Andrew Carlson  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     TISSUE TAKEN FOR ER RIGHT CHEST WALL SKIN LESION   SENT FOR PERMANENTS O R  Resident  Mary K  Klassen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Randall David Gaz  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  AXILLARY CONTENTS  CHEST WALL SKIN   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
