rogesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm fragment of yellow red  firm breast tissue with localizing wire in place  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm firm  poorly circumscribed stellate lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Representative portion frozen as frozen section  1  now A  The remainder submitted in B through H  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Jeffrey Field Bleakley  M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
