Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  31 MAY 94 at 15 55 CLINICAL DATA  Ductal carcinoma in situ with invasion on biopsy at an outside hospital  reviewed here                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO AND SOLID TYPES  SEVERAL DUCT PROFILES  SEE NOTE  2  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  FIBROSIS AND SIDEROPHAGES  3  SKIN WITH SCAR  SOFT TISSUE AND LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  NOTE  Both the infiltrating and in situ components are confined to the region of the biopsy cavity  which is entirely submitted for histological examination  Infiltrating tumor is present only on slide L  while intraductal tumor is on several slides  Ductal carcinoma in situ spans a region of at least 1 5cm  There is no evidence of lymphatic or vascular invasion  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 04                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   A few tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The tumor cells containing estrogen receptor protein might represent intraductal carcinoma  Invasive carcinomas with these morphological features usually do not display hormone receptors  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate containers  Labeled  Lumpectomy   is a 100 gm lumpectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  containing a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  with a linear healed incision  measuring 2 2cm  A long suture designates lateral and a short suture designates superior  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm thin walled biopsy cavity  present 2 0cm deep to the skin ellipse  and 0 9cm from the deep resection margin  The parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavity is rubbery and white  containing multiple less than 0 2cm bright yellow foci  No other lesions are identified  Labeled  Right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue sectioned to reveal seven rubbery  tan pink lymph nodes  ranging in size from 0 6cm in greatest dimension to 1 6cm in greatest dimension  The nodes are bisected to reveal a tan to tan pink  smooth cut surface  SECTION CODE  A  biopsy cavity with deep resection margin  representative section  B E  biopsy cavity  representative radial sections  F  skin with scar  representative section  G H  unremarkable parenchyma  representative sections  I K  lymph nodes  bisected  one half submitted  L N  biopsy cavity  remainder in entirety  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS   EXCISION   report_end  , Pathologic.
