Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 57 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The largest diameter of the invasive carcinoma as measured on a glass slide is 1 4cm  However  the invasive carcinoma is present in 8 of 12 slides indicating that the carcinoma is present in a significant  approximately 2 3  portion of the biopsy specimen  Thus  the tumor appears to span an area greater than 2 0cm  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT THROUGH ENTIRE TISSUE  INTERMEDIATE AND HIGH GRADE  WITH COMEDO NECROSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  3  THE INTRA OPERATIVE GROSS DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protien  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm segment of fibrofatty breast tissue with localization wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 6cm tan  firm nodular area that extends to within 0 1cm of the inked margin grossly  A second 0 6cm fragment of tan  fibrofatty tissue is present  this is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan yellow unremarkable tissue  The specimens are submitted entirely in cassettes A through L  with suspicious area in A  and the second fragment of tissue entirely in L  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  AREA GROSSLY HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Staff Pathologist  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
