Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  11 MAY 93 at 11 42 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING  75   AND INTRADUCTAL  25   CARCINOMA  1 1 CM   MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Intraductal carcinoma of comedocarcinoma type extensively involves the remaining specimen with cancerization of the lobules and several foci of micro invasion  Areas suspicious for lymphatic invasion are identified  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH DUCT EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  3  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Fiona M  Graeme Cook  M D  Signed On  13 MAY 93 at 15 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 93 at 13 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a localizing wire attached and a specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing streaks of rubbery  white parenchyma admixed with fat and a 1 1cm diameter  irregular area of gray white tissue with a gritty consistency  located next to the thick distal end of the wire and abutting the inked margin  A representative section of the gritty area is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and the block is saved frozen  The remainder of the gritty area is submitted in A and B  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in C through K  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING AND IN SITU DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Anthony Mattia  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
