e value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue with localizing wire and accompanying x ray showing a focus of microcalcifications  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal an ill defined 1 5cm area of white tissue containing scattered cysts  admixed with foci of fleshy pink tan tissue  The lesion is submitted in cassette A through C  and the remainder of the specimen in cassettes D through H  No frozen section is done  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES AND AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Anthony Mattia  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST , Pathologic_size.
