Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 31 CLINICAL DATA  48 year old female with infiltrating ductal carcinoma of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   1   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  1    LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE FOCUS  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE FOCUS  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  SEE NOTE  2   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  1  In areas the tumor has a tubular pattern  The infiltrating ductal carcinoma is within 0 1cm of the inked superior resection margin  The tumor is 0 9cm in greatest dimension no lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  The single focus of LCIS  slide M  is 0 3cm from a superior margin  NOTE  2  The focus of lobular carcinoma in situ is within 0 1cm of the closest inked resection margin  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 20 01 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  in three separately labeled parts  Labeled  left  breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue with 2 attached sutures  a long one designating the lateral aspect and a short one designating the superior aspect  The superior portion is inked green  Sectioning reveals firm  white tan  focally  red and gritty  irregular breast parenchyma extending to the inked margins  A representative section of the firm area 1 5cm from lateral edge is frozen as FX 1  Another firm area  1cm in diameterm  0 1cm from the inked margin  lies adjacent to the short suture is frozen as FX 2  The FX 2 is sent to Cox 5  SECTION CODE  A M  entire breast parenchyma  from superior portion to inferior portion  N  FX 1  lateral margin  Labeled  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal firm  white tan  focally yellow  focally cystic  irregular  cut surfaces  submitted entirely in O through S  Labeled  left axillary contents   is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing several lymph nodes  rangin