ody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of breast tissue  The specimen is inked  and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 8cm  stellate  tan mass adjacent to an inked margin  surrounded by rubbery  white tissue  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1 and saved  The specimen is entirely submitted in A through E  Stellate mass submitted in A and B  Resident  David Andrews  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   RADICAL SCAR VERSUS WELL DIFFERENTIATED ADENOCARCINOMA EXTENDING TO INKED MARGIN  AWAIT PERMANENTS FOR FINAL DIAGNOSIS  O R  Resident  Jay Austen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
