Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 47 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  PLEOMORPHIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA   REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The involved lymph node spans 2 1cm  and the malignant cells extend into axillary fat  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain stain for progresterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 08     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary contents  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a left breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 13 0cm  an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 14 0cm with nipple present  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a purple white  irregularly defined  hard  stellate mass  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm which comes to within 1 0cm of the inferior margin  1 5cm within the superior margin  and 2 5cm to the deep margin  Within the axillary tail are ten  tan  rubbery nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Section Code  A  tumor to inferior margin B  tumor to superior margin C  tumor to deep margin D  tumor to skin E  representative section of tumor F  representative section of normal breast GandH  each contain two nodules  each from the axillary tail I N  contains halves of nodules  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 40 CLINICAL DATA  45 year old female with left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  25    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  75    ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE   LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIFOCAL  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The infiltrating and in situ ductal carcinoma measures 2 5cm  in diameter as measured on the glass slides  and is extensively present in the tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity  Both ductal and lobular carcinoma in situ are present in breast parenchyma separate from the biopsy site  The deep resection margin is negative  FIBROADENOMA  SMALL  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 13 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two separately labeled parts  Labeled  left breast  stitch on top of axillary contents   is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  11 x REMOVED_DATE x 4cm  with an attached 13 x 5 5cm skin ellipse  and 9 x 2 x 1 5cm axillary tail  The skins contains a 2 2cm curved scar located 1cm superolateral to the nipple  Specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm irregular cavity located 0 4cm deep to the scar and extending to within 1cm of the nearest deep margin  Cavity is filled with red brown hemorrhage and surrounded by focally gritty tan yellow tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma is rubbery  tan white  and contains numerous cysts ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in diameter  The axillary tail contains several  approximately 6  soft red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 5cm in diameter  SECTION CODE  A  biopsy cavity including nearest deep margin B D  representative biopsy cavity E G  representative breast parenchyma H  representative nipple IandJ  lymph nodes from axillary tail  Labeled  highest left axillary nodes  stitch on highest   is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing multiple  approximately 7   soft tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are submitted in K through M  node adjacent to stitch in M   Resident  Anthony Mattia  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST and AXILLARY CONTENTS PART B  HIGHEST AXILLARY NODES   report_end  , Pathologic.
