as of tan firmness surrounding  No discrete masses or lesions are identified  The specimen is submitted entirely from medial to lateral in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the section containing the slightly firmer tissue adjacent to the central hemorrhage in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the section containing the metal clip in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    M J   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior final shaved margins   are multiple fragments of tan pink  shaggy to shiny soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm in aggregate  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan pink  unremarkable cut surface  and is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  medial final shaved margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of tan pink to yellow  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior final shaved margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of pink brown  shiny to shaggy  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lateral shaved final margins   are two fragments of tan brown to pink  shiny to shaggy  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm in aggregate  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   are two fragments of red orange  shiny fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  Nine candidate lymph nodes ranging in greatest dimension from 0 2cm to 1 2cm  are identified  The candidate lymph nodes are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four candidate lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional left axilla contents   are multiple fragments of tan yellow  fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm in aggregate  Two lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE and 1 3cm in greatest dimension respectively  are identified  The specimen is submitted entirely as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Attached fibroadipose tissue  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART F  LYMPH NODE  LEFT A  report_end  , Pathologic_size.
