Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 11 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SINGLE FOCUS REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 7 OF 7 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a simple mastectomy specimen containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm irregularly shaped  white  firm mass with white fibrous strands radiating away from the center  The mass appears to be located mainly in the anterior and inferior portion of the resected specimen  A second firm mass is located approximately 1 5cm lateral and 1cm superior to the previously described mass  The second mass has a 0 5cm brown colored core surrounded by 0 1cm light tan colored shell  The second mass is located at 1 2cm away from the posterior deep resection margin  SECTION CODE A  Section of first tumor mass at its closest margin  anterior inferior margin   B  Body of the first tumor mass  C  Section containing the second tumor mass on the lateral side near the deep  posterior  resection margin  D  Another section containing the center of the second mass  E  Section on the lateral end of the specimen containing some fibrous tissue at the posterior resection margin  Seven lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  ranging in size from 0 5cm up to 2 2cm in length  The four larger nodes are bisected in half and the three smaller nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes F to H  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Randall David Gaz  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Pathologic.
