Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 MAY 94 at 11 45 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  PHYLLOIDES TUMOR  LOW GRADE  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN A TINY FOCUS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 8cm in greatest dimension and displays moderate stromal cellularity  In regions  the tumor has an infiltrative border  and the tumor cells extend to the margin of the specimen in one small area  The tumor cells do not show either atypia or mitotic activity  Stromal overgrowth is not present  These findings suggest a low likelihood for recurrence and metastasis  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 MAY 94 at 12 18                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal a fairly well demarcated lesion  REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in maximum dimension and extending to within 1mm of the inked margin  The lesion is tan gray  bulging and mobile  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  submitted in cassette L  A section representing the lesion with the closest margin is submitted in cassette A  the lesion in cassettes B through G  remainder of the specimen is cassettes H through K  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  FAVOR BENIGN  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Christopher S Ogilvy  M D  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
