rogesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 94 at 14 48     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm breast biopsy with a short stitch marking superior and a long stitch marking lateral  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a hard  gritty  white brown stellate shaped mass  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm  located 0 5cm from the anterior resection margin closest  5 0cm from the superior resection margin  7 0cm from the lateral resection margin  3 5cm from the medial resection margin  and 1 5cm from the deep resection margin  The remainder of the specimen is noted for large areas of normal appearing soft tan breast parenchyma and adipose tissue  SECTION CODE  A  superior resection margin  en face B  lateral resection margin  en face C  inferior resection margin  en face D  medial resection margin  en face E  deep resection margin  radial F  tumor and anterior resection margin  closest G  section of tumor  disregard inked margin  artifact H  deep resection margin and cystic area  adjacent to tumor I  tumor and anterior resection margin J  representative normal breast  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm mass of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  Lymph nodes  11  measuring up to 3 0cm in greatest dimension are dissected and submitted in cassettes K through Q  Also received  label