Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 06 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass  DCIS on needle localization  previous right breast biopsy at outside hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  40    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  60    WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is present adjacent to the biopsy cavity and extends inferiorly to within 0 4cm  of the inked margin  The carcinoma is 1 2cm in greast dimension  There is no unequivocal vascular nor lymphatic invasion  2 BIOPSY SITE  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 56                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Wide excision  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm fragment of breast with a 4 x 0 3cm overlying skin ellipse  which displays a 0 4cm long central scar  Two sutures  one long  one short  are present and provide orientation  The specimen is inked in black and the inferior aspect is additionally inked in yellow  A REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 5cm blood filled cavity is present 1 1cm deep to the skin and approaches to 1cm of the deep margin  The cavity is lined by firm  and focally hard  yellow tissue  Inferior to the cavity  extending to the inferior resection margin  is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm rubbery  white region  Superior to the cavity is soft to rubbery fibroadipose tissue  SECTION CODE  A   scar with underlying biopsy cavity B   lateral margin  inferior portion C   medial margin D through L   sections of the biopsy cavity and surrounding tissue  from lateral to medial  including rubbery white area  Resident  Andrea Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
