Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 22 CLINICAL DATA  Needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM DIAMETER  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95   EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   NOTE  No lymphatic or venous invasion is noted  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH FOCAL COMEDO CHANGE  5    3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast lump   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm red and yellow  soft tissue fragment with a localizing needle and accompanying mammogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined  spiculated  firm  yellow to white mass  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm that abuts the inked resection margin  The nodule is submitted in cassettes A through C and the remaining specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes D through J  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST LUMP   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
