receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 19     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 neu AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  LEFT   Fifteen percent of the tumor cells stain fro HER 2 neu  Unfavoarable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 MAY 98 at 13 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 1 0cm in diameter nodule sectioned to reveal a 0 7cm diameter somewhat firm  tan  well defined nodule approaching a margin and suspicious for invasive carcinoma  A touch preparation is suggestive of carcinoma and a small piece frozen as frozen section  1 at Dr  Carter s request  Remainder entirely in A and B  frozen in C  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
