Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 MAY 95 at 12 44 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal density on radiograph                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA WITH FEATURES OF BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA  75    2  CARCINOMA IN SITU  DUCTAL AND LOBULAR TYPES  25    3  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  4  FIBROADENOMA   SEE NOTE   NOTE  If this were graded as a ductal carcinoma  it would conform to grade REMOVED_DATE The tumor measures 1 5cm in greatest dimension  however  all ten slides examined  including the separate smaller breast nodule  contain tumor  Carcinoma is present at multiple inked margins  Vessel invasion is not identified  Hormone receptor stains will be reported as an addendum  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Left breast lesion  are two fragments of breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The largest piece is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of stellate  gritty tissue  A representative section FX 1  saved frozen to Cox 5  Representative sections A H   gritty area  cassettes A B   A small fragment is inked and sectioned to reveal a fibrous parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in I and J  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST LESION   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
