Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 12 12 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  WITH A MAXIMUM SPAN OF REMOVED_DATE CM  MEASURED FROM SLIDES B AND C   EXTENDING TO AN INKED CAUTERIZED MARGIN ACROSS A BROAD FRONT  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   HEALING ASPIRATION SITE  NOTE  By immunoperoxidase methods  the infiltrating tumor cells stain strongly for cytokeratin  but show unconvincing to faint non membrane staining for e cadherin  consistent with the morphological impression of lobular carcinoma  A small population of e cadherin negative cells within ducts have a similar cytological appearance  The invasive tumor cells are widely scattered in fibrous parenchyma and mostly dispersed as single cells  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 17 18                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block B   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  01 AUG 03 at 14 28     FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION Addendum     RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block B   HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 03 at 17 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is firm and somewhat rubbery on palpation  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal firm  tan white tissue admixed with softer yellow adipose tissue  The specimen is taken entirely in cassettes A C  Resident  MINDY J  HULL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 14 CLINICAL DATA  80 year old female with breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE CELLULAR MUCINOUS CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of carcinoma  The tumor displays endocrine characteristics  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm simple mastectomy specimen containing a REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm unremarkable skin ellipse with an unremarkable centrally placed nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  gritty  tan tissue mass that extends up to the overlying skin ellipse and to within 0 8cm of the nearest deep margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  No axillary tail is present  Section code  A  tumor with closest deep margin  representative section B  skin with tumor  representative section C F tumor  representative sections G  nipple  trisected  in entirety H  unremarkable parenchyma  representative sections Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  COMP  BREAST HEALTH CENTER REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
