dipose  This area of firm tissue is REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and is somewhat similar in appearance to the tissue immediately beneath the biopsy site  This focus  however  is not in continuity with the biopsy site  and extends to within 1 5cm of the nearest margin  which is deep and slightly superior  The remaining breast parenchyma is composed mostly of adipose  with fine white  linear streaking  no other masses and no other cysts  The axillary tail contains multiple firm  tan white nodules which may represent lymph node  measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in length  the larger lymph nodes with fatty replacement  Section Code A   nipple and red skin lesion B C   skin with biopsy site and underlying firm tissue D G   hematoma site with surrounding tissue and nearest margin H J   representative breast parenchyma including all quadrants K O   lymph nodes Resident  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  OR ROOM UNKNOWN REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  James M Fitzgerald  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY    report_end  , Pathologic.
