ned with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast and axillary nodes  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of breast and axillary tail  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm skin ellipse overlying the specimen  There is a 1 5cm diameter nipple present on the skin ellipse  The nipple appears unremarkable  1 0cm inferior and 2 0cm lateral to the skin ellipse is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  focally well circumscribed mass with a tan gritty cut surface  The mass extends to 0 1cm of the deep margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is focally firm and white with areas of fibrofatty tissue  The axillary nodes are as large as 1 5cm in diameter and firm and pink  Section Code  A  mass  deep margin  B  mass  anterior margin  C D  mass  anterior and deep margin  D  mass  E J  representative sections of breast  K R  nodes from axillary tail  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY SPECIMEN   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
