Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 01 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM   98   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  2    NOTE  The tumor extends to the inked margin  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Focal microcalcifications are identified in adjacent  non tumorous breast tissue  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 06                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST  RIGHT BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   2   Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 43     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab is a 2 x 2 x 1cm specimen of fibroadipose tissue incised and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm gritty  stellate nodule  abutting the margin  A thin slice of the specimen is placed in medium for cycle studies and the remainder is entirely submitted in A F  Gross Description by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD Resident  Jason Lockridge  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  SMALL NODULE SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
