g of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right breast  is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a poorly defined  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  white tan mass that extends to within 0 2cm of the margin  Tissue is frozen for estrogen receptors and the frozen section block is saved frozen  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A F   remainder of tumor with adjacent margins G I   representative surrounding tissue Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST BIOPSY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Anthony Mattia  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Wiley Souba  MD PART   BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
