 binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass   with attached specimen x ray   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing no gross lesion large enough to freeze  A 0 7cm ill  defined  slightly firm and gritty area is present at an inked margin  The nodule is submitted entirely in A through C  the remainder of the tissue in D through N  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS GROSS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   NO LESION LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
