Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 11 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast calcifictions  mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU INVOLVING MOST OF THE SPECIMEN AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN IN SEVERAL FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 6cm diameter firm ill defined mass located 0 2cm from the closest inked margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in A G  with the nodule in A and B  Resident  TAN A  INCE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   A REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIAMETER FIRM NODULE  TO SMALL TO FREEZE   O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
