ive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal firm  white tissue with focal areas of gritty calcification  An accompanying specimen xray show abundant calcifications  A representative section of the gritty  calcified tissue is frozen as FX  1  now A  The remainder submitted in B R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS , Pathologic_size.
