Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT BREAST MASS    EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   PRESENT AT AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES ALONG A BROAD FRONT AND INVOLVING A RADIAL SCAR   SEE NOTE  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Ductal carcinoma in situ is present in 3 of 10 slides  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 05                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  It is incised and sectioned to reveal breast parenchyma with multiple  focal  rubbery  nodular areas  No frozen section is done  Representative sections are submitted in cassette A through J  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST MASS   NO LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
