 The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends 0 19cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus and is   0 2cm from all other examined margins  Stains for receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE WITH NO EVIDENCE OF METASTATIC CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   ATYPICAL LYMPHOPLASMACYTIC INFILTRATE  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  There is an atypical lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate which is suspicious for involvement by low grade B cell lymphoma  Additional studies are in progress to address this possibility  and the results will be reported in an addendum  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1  BREAST LUMP  MAMMARY CARCINOMA  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lump   is a REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 3cm lumpectomy specimen with a short stitch indicating anterior  a long stitch indicating lateral  and a bowtie indicating superior  The anterior is inked blue  posterior black  superior  green  inferior  yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm firm nodule in the middle of the specimen that has a 0 5cm cystic area  The nodule is within 0 6cm from the anterior margin  1 9cm from the posterior margin  0 9cm from the inferior margin  and roughly 1 5cm from the superior margin  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as FX 1  and submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The rest of the nodule is submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four additional sections of the specimen are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 7cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing a potential node  The specimen is quadrisected and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show focally moderate overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Note  Immunohistochemical stains for kappa and lambda light chain demonstrate a polytypic population of plasma cells in the sentinel lymph node  Scattered plasma cells express IgM  but they are a small minority of the overall plasma cell population  These results do not confirm the presence of involvement by the patient s known marginal zone B cell lymphoma  However  the node remains suspicious for involvement based on the histologic features  i e   a lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate composed of numerous plasma cells showing occasional slightly immature nuclei and rare Dutcher bodies  and monocytoid lymphocytes with slightly irregular nuclei infiltrating germinal centers  If clinically indicated  additional studies could be performed for a more definitive diagnosis  Addendum  2 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  801  to chromosome 17 signals  133  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  3 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION , Pathologic_size.
