edictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  yellow red and tan  fibrofatty lumpectomy specimen  which is inked and sectioned to reveal fatty tissue  with a 1 0cm focal white firm area adjacent to the inked resection margin  A piece of firm area is frozen as FX 1  representative sections of the remaining tissue are submitted in A through J  with FX 1 in K  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Hugh Pollard Chandler  M D  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
