Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 44 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM GREATEST DIMENSION ON TISSUE SECTION  EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  NOTE  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 51                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm portion of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan  firm  stellate lesion that abutts the inked resection margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in A   E  the mass in A   D  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  Katharine Treadway  M D  PART    RIGHT  BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
