Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 19 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer by core biopsy performed at an outside hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING FOCALLY TO AN INKED  ANTERIOR  MARGIN  SLIDE F   WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION AT A DISTANCE FROM THE MAIN TUMOR  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  3  HEALING CORE BIOPSY SITE  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION OF ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN  FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS  REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 7 OF 7 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODE  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS  REGIONAL DISSECTION  ONE LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 18 04                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  lumpectomy  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm portion of breast with a short stitch indicating the superior margin  a long stitch indicating the lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  deep margin  black  inferior margin  blue  superior margin  red  and the anterior margin  green  A section is made at the inferior margin to reveal an irregularly defined  firm  white mass measuring 1 2cm in greatest dimension and coming to within 0 1cm from the inferior margin  The specimen is submitted in its entirety from the lateral to medial margin in cassettes A through H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  additional margin inferior cavity  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of fibrofatty yellow tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a grossly unremarkable yellow fatty parenchyma  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes I through M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node contents  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of fibrofatty tissue from which multiple tan pink lymph nodes ranging in length from 0 3cm to 1 5cm in length are dissected away  The nodes are submitted in cassettes M through P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional node cont