Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 19 21 CLINICAL DATA  Prior left lumpectomy with axillary dissection for DCIS with invasion  negative nodes but positive margins on lumpectomy  Now for completion simple mastectomy and TRAM reconstruction                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT WITHIN THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  2  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III    SEE NOTE   NOTE  A separate invasive carcinoma is present 4 0cm superior to the original carcinoma  This second focus of invasive carcinoma is at least 1 0cm and displays several small satellite foci of invasion   0 3cm   adjacent to the main tumor mass  The second focus of invasive carcinoma most likely represents a second intramammary primary  however an intramammary metastasis can not be excluded  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  ER PR will be reported in an addendum  The margins are free of invasive carcinoma  3  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  MULTICENTRIC  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The ductal carcinoma in situ extends away from the invasive carcinoma and is present in multiple tissue sections  4 FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR BIOPSY SITE  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 34                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  name and unit number and  left breast  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with an REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm overlying skin ellipse displaying a REMOVED_DATE long scar on the lateral side  The specimen is inked and sectioned  An obvious biopsy cavity site is not seen grossly  Several areas of firm  white fibrous tissue are identified  the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm abutting the posterior resection margin  this area is located beneath the nipple  Another ill defined  firm white area is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and abuts a posterior inked margin is adjacent to the lateral stitch  and 0 5cm from the first fibrotic area  A third area  which is very ill defined consisting of firm  white fibrous tissue measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and abuts the posterior inked margin  this area is 4 0cm superior to the first fibrotic area and is adjacent to the superior stitch  Section code  A D representative sections of the  first  fibrotic area beneath the nipple  EandF fibrotic tissue adjacent to long lateral stitch  G K representative sections of fibrous tissue in the most superior region  LandM fibrous area  measuring 0 9cm in greatest dimension intramedial to the nipple  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Pathologic.
