Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  26 MAY 94 at 14 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  LARGER SPECIMEN   TUBULAR CARCINOMA SPANNING ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA MICROPAPILLARY CRIBRIFORM TYPE  PRESENT IN TWO OF NINETEEN SECTIONS AND HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The margins of the specimen appear free of invasive and in situ carcinoma  Invasion of blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The intraoperative impression is confirmed  BREAST  RIGHT  SMALLER SPECIMEN   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  SMALL FOCI PRESENT IN TWO OF FIVE SECTIONS  RADIAL SCAR  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  FIBROSIS  ATROPHY  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  MICROCYST FORMATION  AND DUCTAL TYPE EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The margins of the specimen appear free of carcinoma  Invasion of stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 18                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  LARGER SPECIMEN   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number only are two pieces of breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  with detached wires  Stitches are present in the larger piece  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm in maximum diameter  tan  slightly firm area located near the stitches and abutting an inked resection margin  The rest of the larger piece as well as the entire smaller piece is predominantly composed of unremarkable adipose tissue and breast parenchyma  No frozen done  Representative sections of larger piece submitted in A through J  with the lesion in A D  entire smaller piece in K through O  Remainder of larger specimen in P through X  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Ta