Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 50 CLINICAL DATA  59 year old female with core biopsy positive for carcinoma of the right breast  now undergoing right lumpectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MEASURED FROM SECTION C   GRADE 1 OF 3  WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE CLOSEST MARGINS  SUPERIOR AND INFERIOR   PRESENT ON THREE OF TEN SLIDES  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SINGLE FOCUS ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE TUMOR  AWAY FROM MARGINS   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  SINGLE FOCUS WITHIN THE SUBCAPSULAR SINUS OF ONE OF NINETEEN LYMPH NODES  LEVELS EXAMINED   Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 33                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone recptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lump  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a fragment of breast tissue measuring 6 x 6 x 1cm that is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1cm in largest diameter stellate  firm to gritty area in a lateral portion of the specimen  0 4cm from the closest margin  the posterior margin   Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial in A through J  B through F contains the entire nodule   The specimen was over inked blue on the posterior margin and green over the superior margin  yellow over the inferior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of adipose tissue  Lymph node dissection is performed with lymph nodes submitted in cassettes K through Q  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST EXCISION   MARGINS FREE OF TUMOR  GROSS ONLY  O R  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA    report_end  , Pathologic_size.
