Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 16 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  SPINDLE CELL CARCINOMA  ADENOCARCINOMA WITH PSEUDOSARCOMATOUS METAPLASIA   REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SCANT WITH FOCAL SQUAMOUS FEATURES AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  3  INTRADUCTAL HYPEPLASIA  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The malignant spindle cells stain for keratin  AE REMOVED_DATE  CAM 5 2  and vimentin  and are negative for desmin  thus supporting the diagnosis of spindle cell carcinoma  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Ref  Wargotz et al  Human Pathology  REMOVED_CASE_ID   volume 20  page REMOVED_DATE Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 12     ELECTRON MICROSCOPY Addendum          ELECTRON MICROSCOPY    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       RIGHT BREAST  SARCOMATOID CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The neoplasm is composed of oval and spindle cells  most of which contain abundant dilated rough endoplasmic reticulum and focal collections of filaments with dense bodies  characteristic of fibroblasts and myofibroblasts  Some of the oval cells contain filaments and tonofibils  consistent with squamous differentiation  Most interesting is that some of the spindle cells show both lines of differentiation  fibroblastic and myofibroblastic on one hand and squamous differentiation on the other  We have seen this phenomenon in other examples of sarcomatoid carcinoma  1   1  Balercia G  Bhan AK  Dickersin GR  Sarcomatoid carcinoma  an ultrastructural study with light microscopic and immunohistochemical correlation of 10 cases from various anatomic sites  Ultrastruct Pathol  REMOVED_CASE_ID   19 249 263  Added by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a 5 x 3 x 1cm segment of breast mass  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 2 x 2 x 2 5cm firm  tan white  diffuse mass on cut sections  A representative section frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  The entire specimen is submitted from A to M  O and P  no block N submitted  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SPINDLE CELL PROLIFERATION OF UNCERTAIN MALIGNANCY POTENTIAL  FAVOR CARCINOMA  DEFER FOR PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Pathologic_size.
