sterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with an needle localizing wire in place and an accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm tan  firm  focally gritty stellate lesion that approaches the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved as frozen  The remaining specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through H  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT MASS  BIOPSY  CARCINOMA WITH LOBULAR FEATURES  HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
