Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 43 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  80    REMOVED_DATE CM MEASURED FROM SLIDES  GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING FOCALLY TO A MARGIN  NO LYMPHATIC OR VASCULAR INVASION IS IDENTIFIED  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  20    HIGH GRADE  WITH COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS  ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT TO A MARGIN  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 43     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a needle localization  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm in diameter tan white stellate firm mass abutting the inked margin  Representative sections of the mass are frozen as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in cassette G  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A   F  with the lesion in cassette C  and again the frozen section in cassette G  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  BREAST MASS  LEFT   PREDOMINANTLY INFILTRATING DUCTAL AND LESS EXTENSIVE INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST MASS  LEFT    report_end  , Pathologic_size.
