Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 44 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT    1    BIOPSY    INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED 98     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  LESS THAN 2     SEE NOTE  1  NOTE  1  The tumor measures 0 9cm in greatest dimension on histologic section and is present at multiple inked resection margins  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Immunohistochemical stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be reported as an addendum  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST  LEFT    2    BIOPSY    NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA   SEE NOTE  2  NOTE  2  The frozen section gross impression is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 33                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two parts  Labeled  Left breast  1  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a white firm nodule 1cm in greatest dimension  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  now N  The remainder of this specimen is submitted entirely in A through J  with the nodule in A through C  Labeled  Left breast  2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 2cm fimr tan nodule  The specimen is submitted entirely in K through M  with the nodule in K  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT   1 EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT   2 EXCISION  SUSPICIOUS LESION IS TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A   1 LEFT BREAST PART B   2 LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
