ining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  A  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan red soft tissue fragment containing a 1 0cm lymph node  bisected  and submitted entirely in cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  B  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm tan yellow breast resection specimen with a long stitch marking the lateral and short stitch marking the superior border of the specimen  The specimen is entirely inked black  the superior surface is overinked blue  the anterior is overinked orange  and posterior surface is overinked green  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm in diameter tan gray firm nodule 0 2cm from the closest  inferior  soft tissue resection margin  Section code  B C  Nodule and the closest resection margin  D F  The tumor nodule submitted entirely  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
