Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 45 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3   MUCINOUS TYPE  0 4 CM   5   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  DCIS   SOLID TYPE AND FOCAL COMEDO TYPE  95   WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  2  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DCIS ARE PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  NO VASCULAR OR LYMPHATIC INVASION ARE SEEN  SEE NOTE  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING MODERATE EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  MICROCYSTS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  4  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  5  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  NOTE  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the case and concurs  Diagnosis by  Julie Fanburg  MD Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 06 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  05 MAY 94 at 11 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm piece of fatty soft tissue  with a localizing wire in place  An x ray accompanies this specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal several REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm firm  tan nodules  The entire specimen is submitted in A through J  with nodules in A through C  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SEVERAL SMALL  0 1 0 3 CM  NODULES  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS TO ASSESS THE POSSIBILITY OF CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
