Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 24 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE I  FORMING TWO NODULES REMOVED_DATE CM AND REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The two nodules appear identical histologically and therefore probably represent independent foci of invasion originating from a single neoplastic population  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 13 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of breast with an indistinct firm area and a localizing wire in place   No accompanying radiograph   Sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular tan firm lesion  extending to within 0 5cm of surface ink  There is adjacent parenchymal hemorrhage  Sections of mass in A through D  with other representative sections in E through J  Received labeled  left axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fatty tissue containing multiple tan rubbery lymph node as large as 1 1cm  submitted in cassettes K through N  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST EXCISION PART B  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
