t of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm breast tissue fragment which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE tan white  firm  stellate mass extending to the resection margins  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  The remainder is submitted entirely in A through I  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CA AND DCIS  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  Ross Charles Wheeler  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
