rgin  The rest of the breast parenchyma contains approximately 20  tan white fibrous tissue and 80  tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No discrete mass is identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire fibrotic area to include inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous tissue  lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous tissue  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  upper outer quadrant tissues that may represent lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 12 o clock position  The overlying tan brown REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm skin ellipse contains a grossly unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm flatten nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  This specimen is serially sectioned along medial to lateral axis to reveal two fibrous scars  The first REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan white  stellate shaped fibrous scar in the outer lower quadrant grossly abuts the anterior inked margin and lies 1 0cm from the posterior inked margin  Approximately 4 5cm medial to this area there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink to tan white  stellate shaped fibrous scar present in the lower inner quadrant which lies 2 0cm from anterior inked margin and 0 4cm from posterior inked margin  The breast parenchyma surrounding the first stellate scar is tan white and nodular  The intervening parenchyma between the 2 scars shows diffuse tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The rest of the breast parenchyma shows minimal fibrous tissue  No discrete mass is identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire first fibrotic area to include closest inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tan white nodular breast parenchyma surroun