Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with an overlying ellipse of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white irregularly defined area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm that abuts the deep and lateral margins  The closest lateral margin in A  deep margin in B  C  J are representative sections of the firm area  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary contents  is a portion of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm  There are six rubbery nodules  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The nodules are entirely submitted in cassettes K and L  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
