say  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm lumpectomy specimen  oriented with a short suture at the superior margin and a long suture at the lateral margin  Entire surface is inked black and the inferior surface is again inked yellow  Sectioning of the specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm round  white  firm and gritty nodule  0 2cm from the inferior resection margin  A representative portion is frozen as FX 1  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast   are two fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  of fibroadipose tissue with an unremarkable tan and yellow mottled cut surface  SECTION CODE A H  breast lump  entirely submitted  serially progressing lateral to medial   B and C represent posterior and anterior portion of one section  respectively  cassettes D and E represent the posterior and anterior portions of the adjacent section  respectively  The frozen section was taken from the section in cassette F   I J  additional inferior margin  towards anterior  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  BREAST  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN    report_end  , Pathologic_size.
