Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 01 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  SCANT  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 21 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of breast with an incision into the specimen  The specimen is inked such that only the true margins bear ink  Inspection reveals an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm tan  firm  lobulated  well circumscribed mass with central and eccentric white stellate lesion which grossly approaches several margins  The tissue surrounding the mass is white and irregularly dense  Entire mass and representative surrounding tissue are submitted in cassettes A J  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST MASS  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
