ry  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a 350 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of breast and axillary tissue with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm  The skin ellipse contains a 5 5cm curvilinear non healed incision  Deep to the incision is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm biopsy cavity  lined with yellow fat and red hemorrhage  Sectioning of the breast reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm poorly demarcated  irregular  firm white mass adjacent to the biopsy cavity  The mass is close to the deep margin and close to the superior medial margin  extending from one to the other  It is 1 4cm deep to the skin at 1 0cm from the medial resection margin  A photograph is taken of the extension from superior medial to deep resection margin  Laterally the tumor infiltrates fat  Throughout the mass are focal hemorrhages  Within the superior medial aspect of tumor are multiple firm white nodules  ranging in diameter from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm  The axillary tail contains multiple firm lymph nodes  SECTION CODE  AandB  skin with tumor and biopsy cavity C E  tumor with biopsy cavity and superior inked margin F I  tumor with deep resection margin J N  tumor with superomedial resection margin O  lateral tumor with infiltration fat P  medial most resection margin Q S  cross section of tumor  representative section T  representative section of lateral parenchyma  grossly uninvolved U  representative section of inferior parenchyma  grossly uninvolve