 for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and designated  L breast mass   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x4 0cm oriented fragment of breast  The superior aspect is inked black  the inferior aspect inked blue  and the posterior surface overinked orange  Much of the parenchyma is replaced by an ill defined  white  firm  stellate lesion which spans approximately 6 0cm in length  and REMOVED_DATE to 5 0cm in diameter  The lesion is partially cystic  and notable for multiple small 0 1cm soft yellow foci  The tumor margins blend in with surrounding firm and focally cystic parenchyma  The lesion grossly abuts the inferior and posterior medial margins  and is within 0 1cm of the superior  anterior and lateral margins  In the inferior portion of the specimen  there is a 1 3cm in greatest diameter  well circumscribed  rubbery firm  tan  and partially cystic nodule which abuts the inferior inked resection surface  A representative section of this nodule is frozen as fx 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  and the remainder is submitted in B D including adjacent slightly firm and cystic parenchyma  Sections are then submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes E S   E G are firm cystic parenchyma medial to lesion  and S contains radial lateral sections   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in six parts  Labeled  additional medial inferior margin   are two unoriented breast fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm in aggregate  with multifocal firm  white and partially cystic parenchyma  extending to the inked surfaces  Representative sections of suspicious margins are in T W  Labeled  additional margin short sup  long new lat margin   is a oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast fragment  the sutured new lateral margin is inked black  and the remaining opposing surface is inked blue  There is an approximately 2 0cm in greatest diameter nodular rubbery firm  white mass midway along the specimen  extending along the new lateral aspect where it abuts the overlying black inked surface  The parenchyma adjacent to and inferior in the specimen is firm and multicystic with white nodular areas  These changes span REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm area  and grossly abut the new inked lateral margin in the inferior aspect of the specimen  Representative sections of the more superiorly located mass are submitted in X Y  with representative sections of the inferior firm parenchyma in Z BB  Labeled  sup margin  additional   S superior and long lateral   is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm breast fragment which is previously partially excised into  The entire specimen is inked black  with the new superior margin overinked blue  The parenchyma is fatty and unremarkable  and approximately half of the specimen is submitted laterally to medially in cassette CC HH  Labeled  final shaved   are multiple breast fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in aggregate  with a partially firm white and focally cystic parenchyma  Also noted are small soft yellow foci  The fragments are submitted entirely in cassettes II VV  Labeled  left axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fatty fragment with multiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 4cm  two of which are tan white and firm  in cassettes WW ZZ  Labeled  additional axillary content   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate of small fatty fragments with small unremarkable lymph nodes  in cassette AAA  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST INFEROMEDIAL NODULE   CONSISTENT WITH MYXOID FIBROADENOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE SUPERIOR  ANTERIOR AND POSTEROMEDIAL MARGIN  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN  PART C  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL LATERAL MARGIN  PART D  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN  PART E  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED  PART F  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  PART G  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL  , Pathologic_size.
