Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 40 CLINICAL DATA  Stitch at deepest portion along the bottom of the specimen                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT  AND  RIGHT INFERIOR PIECE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  PREDOMINANTLY LOBULAR BUT ALSO WITH DUCTAL DIFFERENTIATION AND WITH EXTENSIVE INVOLVEMENT OF BIOPSY MARGINS  BOTH SPECIMENS   THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  LOBULAR CARCINOMA  IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  FOCAL FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  Diagnosis by  Robert B  Colvin  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 18 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 33     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  in two parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and designated as follows  Labeled  right breast needle localization specimen   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with an attached needle localization wire and a stitch designating the deep aspect  A specimen X ray accompanies the specimen  The deep aspect of the specimen is inked yellow and sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular  firm  white tan stellate mass extending to the inked lateral and deep margins  A representative section is submitted as FX 1 and the block is saved frozen   Note  no orientation is provided for anatomic medial and lateral orientation of the specimen   The breast tissue away from the main tumor mass shows nodular  yellow white  firm to rubbery fibrous appearing tissue that is also present along the lateral and deep margin  Representative sections from the region of the tumor mass are submitted in cassettes A through C  Representative sections extending across the base of the specimen in the regions of the nodular white rubbery areas are submitted in cassettes D through G  Labeled  inferior piece right breast  outside of tumor   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular  firm  white tan stellate portion of the parenchyma  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  This lesion extends to inked margin  A representative section is submitted as FX 2 and the block is saved frozen  Representative sections are submitted for permanent sections in cassettes H through J  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST  MAIN SPECIMEN   INFILTRATING AND IN SITU CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2   RIGHT BREAST  INFERIOR PIECE   INFILTRATING AND IN SITU CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  OZDEMIRLI METIN  NO ADDRESS  O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  Carolyn Diana Jordan  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST PART B  RIGHT BREAST INFERIOR PIECE   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
