Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  17 MAY 94 at 14 37 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 8 CM   WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 1 3   95   AND DCIS  5   INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   NOTE  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  2  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  20 MAY 94 at 16 46 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 94 at 14 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast biopsy specimen with a localizing wire in place  An x ray accompanies this specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  tan  ill defined  stellate gritty lesion 0 1cm from the nearest inked resection margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in A through G  with the lesion in A through D  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   SCLEROSING LESION 8MM IN DIAMETER SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Douglas Brian Flieder  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
