Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 46 CLINICAL DATA  Diagnosis by FNA  positive EPR                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  A focus of metastatic carcinoma spanning about 1 0cm involves the axillary tissue surrounding one lymph node  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 26                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 30 x 18 x 3cm mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the superior margin  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 4 5cm in diameter mass which is superior to the nipple and is ill defined  firm  and gritty and measuring 1 7cm from the closest  posterior  margin  SECTION CODE A  Tumor with closest  deep  margin  B D  Representative sections of tumor  E F  Representative tissue away from the tumor  G I  LN Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
