Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 36 CLINICAL DATA  Calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  SCATTERED SMALL NODULES AND CELL CLUSTERS AGGREGATING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OR LESS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  INVOLVING THE ENTIRE SPECIMEN  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN MANY FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm unoriented piece of fibroadipose tissue with multiple needle localization wires  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm  white nodule that grossly abuts the margin and several smaller nodules ranging from 0 2cm to 0 3cm in diameter  Representative sections are submitted in A through J  Gross Description by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Resident  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST   LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
