Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 AUG 96 ACCESSIONED ON  14 AUG 96 at 10 12 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III   EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  AND WITH FOCI HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  SEE NOTE  Note  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE AND HIGH GRADE  WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE CARCINOMA  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  3  FOCAL LACTATIONAL CHANGE  4  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  19 AUG 96 at 09 46                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 96 at 09 26     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 6 x 4 x 2cm portion of fibrofatty tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  tan yellow circumscribed nodule within firm  white parenchyma  The nodule is within 0 2cm of the margin  A portion of the nodule is frozen as FX  1 and submitted in cassette M  The remainder of the nodule is submitted in cassettes A through E  The parenchyma in its entirely in F through L  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST BIOPSY  LEFT    report_end  , Pathologic_size.
