Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  22 AUG 94 at 11 25 CLINICAL DATA  History of intraductal carcinoma in the left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATIED GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95   REMOVED_DATE CM MAXIMAL DIAMETER AT SURGICAL RESECTION MARGIN  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 2  FIBROSIS WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND TYPICAL AND ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Dr  Ferguson aware of diagnosis at 9 30 AM ON August 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  26 AUG 94 at 14 57 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  with localizing wire in place  A mammogram accompanies the specimen which demonstrates faint microcalcifications towards the distal end of the wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a pale tan fibrous nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and scattered blue cysts  0 2cm in maximum diameter  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through J  with the nodular area in cassette D  areas around the terminal wire in cassettes A through E  and cystic areas in cassettes F through J  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   NO LESIONS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
