Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3 3  APPROACHING MULTIPLE INKED AND CAUTERIZED RESECTION MARGINS  NO LYMPHATIC OR VASCULAR INVASION IS IDENTIFIED  SEE NOTE  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH EXTENSIVE SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA AND ATYPICAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  3  FIBROADENOMA  NOTE  Architectural distortion due to extensive cautery prevents an accurate assessment of margins and the relative contributions of invasive and in situ components  It appears  however  that several margins must be considered as potentially positive for invasive carcinoma  and that the invasive component is at least 0 5cm in diameter as measured from the histological slides  Levels on several blocks have been examined  The rapid gross evaluation is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 26 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragmented fibrofatty breast tissue fragment with localizing wire and accompanying X ray showing a vague nodular density  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 2cm gritty retracted area  no frozen is done  Suspicious area is submitted in cassettes A and B  remainder in cassettes C through F  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  SUSPICIOUS AREA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
