MISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 08 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number   right axillary sentinel lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lymph node which is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  now as A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number   right breast  is a piece of fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm in greatest dimensions  oriented with 2 sutures  The specimen is inked black and over inked blue on superior aspect  and green on a anterior aspect  It is cut serially from medial to lateral to reveal a small spiculated lesion  2mm in diameter  The lesion is 1 2cm from lateral margin  0 4cm from the posterior margin  0 2cm from the anterior margin  1 2cm from the inferior margin and 1 2cm from the superior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is fatty and unremarkable  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  B  lateral margin  en face  C  lesion  D I  serial sections lateral to medial  J  medial margin  en face  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axilla lymph nodes  is a fragment of fatty tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Lymph nodes ranging size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm are identified  The lymph nodes are submitted in K L M  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  B  are 3 separate fragments of fat with suture attached to one piece  The specimen is impossible to orient in view of the fragmented nature  The fragment with suture measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and is entirely submitted in N  The other 2 fragments measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and are entirely submitted in O P  Gross Description by  LAURENCE DE LEVAL  MD Resident  VIKRAM DESHPANDE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  RIGHT AXILLARY   METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  4 MM IN DIAMETER  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  BIOPSY SITE REMOVED_DATE CM IN SIZE  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM DEEP MARGIN  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM ANTERIOR MARGIN  NO OTHER LESION GROSSLY IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  LAURENCE DE LEVAL  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART B  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 54 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma with lumpectomy 7 years ago                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is very poorly circumscribed and is REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in cross section  as measured from the slides  It focally extends to within less than 1mm of the resection margin in several foci  A circumscribed nodule of tumor associated with a small rim of lymphocytes is also present  It is not possible to determine if this is a separate tumor nodule  or a small lymph node completely replaced by carcinoma  Extensive lymphatic permeation is present  There is no evidence of an in situ component  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 49                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 02     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with localizing wire in place and accompanying x ray  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  white  well defined 0 6cm nodule  adjacent to a firm  white  0 6cm poorly defined extending to within 0 1cm of the inked margin  A representative section from the area close to the margin is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  A thin sliver sent for BRDU  Lesion submitted in A F  Additional tissue submitted as G and H  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 33 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  WITH FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    LOW GRADE ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS   SEE NOTE   3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The margins are free of ductal carcinoma in situ  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST   NEW MARGIN   EXCISION   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast tissue with short stitch posteriorly  2 pins  long stitch   1 pin  laterally  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm ill defined tan white  firm mass that abuts the lateral margin  Representative section of tumor at the closest  lateral  margin is frozen as FX 1 and the is submitted in cassette A  The extreme posterior margin is submitted in cassette B and the next adjacent section is submitted in cassette C  The posterior margin is double inked with green color and the anterior margin inked black in cassette C   The tumor closest to the closest margin  lateral  is submitted in cassette D  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  new margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty tissue  Long stitch is in the lateral side and the short stitch in the superior side  The old margin is inked in black and the new lateral margin is inked in blue  The superior margin is inked in red  Representative section taken through the old margin and the new margins are presented in cassettes E G  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                              