cs determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of breast tissue with a needle localization wire in place  There is a central  incisional defect within the specimen  The accompanying specimen x ray reveals microcalcifications  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal 60  yellow lobular adipose and 40  dense white fibrous tissues  Within the area of calcifications  the fibrous tissue is coursely granular with ducts exuding a white material  Also received in the same container is an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fatty  yellow  lobular portion of breast tissues  Representative sections are submitted to include all of the fibrous tissue and the area with microcalcifications as A J  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  JHE                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Pathologic_size.
