ith this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 25     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two separate specimens  Labeled  left breast   1    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 2cm in greatest diameter  well circumscribed  stellate  hard nodule that abuts the inked margin  A representative section of this nodule is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Entirely submitted in cassettes in A through F  with nodule in cassettes A through C  Labeled  left breast   2    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal no areas suspicious for carcinoma  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes G through P  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  1  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  2  NO GROSS LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST MASS PART B  LEFT BREAST MASS  2 , Pathologic_size.
